n(RA,"bedbugs","med","Stripping a bed, you spot tiny dark spots and a small reddish bug on the mattress seam. What do you do?","Al quitar las sábanas ves puntitos oscuros y un bichito rojizo en la costura del colchón. ¿Qué haces?",
 ["Stop, leave everything in place, close the door and tell your supervisor right away","Finish cleaning and mention it at end of shift","Spray it with glass cleaner","Move the linens to the next room"],["Detenerte, dejar todo como está, cerrar la puerta y avisarle a tu supervisora de inmediato","Terminar de limpiar y comentarlo al final del turno","Rociarlo con limpiavidrios","Llevar la ropa de cama al siguiente cuarto"],
 "Possible bed bugs: don't carry linens out and spread them. Isolate the room so it can be inspected.","Si pueden ser chinches, no saques la ropa de cama para no regarlas. Aísla el cuarto para que lo revisen.",BED)
n(RA,"bedbugs","hard","Where do bed bugs most often hide in a guest room?","¿Dónde se esconden más seguido las chinches en un cuarto?",
 ["Mattress seams, box spring and headboard","Inside the minifridge","In the shower drain","On the ceiling light"],["En las costuras del colchón, la base y la cabecera","Dentro del minirefrigerador","En la coladera de la regadera","En la lámpara del techo"],
 "Bed bugs stay close to where people sleep: seams, tags, box springs and headboards.","Las chinches se quedan cerca de donde duermen las personas: costuras, etiquetas, bases y cabeceras.",BED)
n(RA,"sharps","easy","You find a used needle in the bedding. What's the safe move?","Encuentras una aguja usada entre las sábanas. ¿Qué es lo seguro?",
 ["Don't touch it — keep others away and call your supervisor for the sharps kit","Pick it up carefully and toss it in the trash","Wrap it in a towel","Put the cap back on"],["No tocarla; alejar a los demás y llamar a tu supervisora para el kit de objetos punzantes","Recogerla con cuidado y tirarla a la basura","Envolverla en una toalla","Ponerle la tapa"],
 "Needles can carry bloodborne disease. Only trained staff with a sharps container and gloves should handle them.","Las agujas pueden transmitir enfermedades por sangre. Solo personal capacitado con guantes y contenedor especial debe manejarlas.",BBP)
n(RA,"blood","med","There's blood on the sheets. What do you wear before handling them?","Hay sangre en las sábanas. ¿Qué te pones antes de tocarlas?",
 ["Disposable gloves, and bag the linen separately per policy","Nothing, just wash hands after","Only an apron","Oven mitts"],["Guantes desechables, y poner la ropa en bolsa aparte según la política","Nada, solo lavarte las manos después","Solo un mandil","Guantes de cocina"],
 "Treat blood as potentially infectious: gloves on, and follow the hotel's soiled-linen procedure.","Trata la sangre como posible fuente de infección: ponte guantes y sigue el procedimiento para ropa sucia.",BBP)
n(RA,"chemicals","med","A spray bottle on your cart has no label. What do you do?","Una botella de tu carrito no tiene etiqueta. ¿Qué haces?",
 ["Don't use it — give it to your supervisor to label or dispose of","Smell it to figure out what it is","Use it on glass only","Mix it with water and use it"],["No usarla; dársela a tu supervisora para etiquetarla o desecharla","Olerla para saber qué es","Usarla solo en vidrios","Mezclarla con agua y usarla"],
 "OSHA requires chemical containers to be labeled so you know the hazards. Unknown chemicals don't get used.","OSHA exige que los químicos estén etiquetados para conocer sus riesgos. Lo que no se sabe qué es, no se usa.",HAZ)
n(RA,"chemicals","med","A cleaner splashes in your eye. What do you do first?","Un limpiador te salpica en el ojo. ¿Qué haces primero?",
 ["Flush with clean water right away, then check the SDS and report it","Rub it","Wait to see if it stops burning","Put lotion on it"],["Enjuagarte con agua limpia de inmediato, luego revisar la SDS y reportarlo","Tallarte el ojo","Esperar a ver si deja de arder","Ponerte crema"],
 "Every chemical has a Safety Data Sheet with first-aid steps. Flush first, then report.","Cada químico tiene su hoja de seguridad (SDS) con primeros auxilios. Primero enjuaga y luego reporta.",HAZ)
n(RA,"ergonomics","easy","What's the safest way to lift a heavy mattress corner to tuck sheets?","¿Cuál es la forma más segura de levantar la esquina de un colchón pesado para meter las sábanas?",
 ["Bend your knees, keep your back straight and use your legs","Bend at the waist and pull fast","Twist while lifting","Lift with one hand"],["Doblar las rodillas, mantener la espalda recta y hacer fuerza con las piernas","Doblarte de la cintura y jalar rápido","Girar mientras levantas","Levantar con una sola mano"],
 "Using your legs and not twisting protects your back on every bed, every day.","Usar las piernas y no girar protege tu espalda en cada cama, todos los días.",LIFT)
n(RA,"ergonomics","med","Your cart is overloaded and hard to push. Best fix?","Tu carrito está sobrecargado y cuesta empujarlo. ¿Qué es lo mejor?",
 ["Unload some and make an extra trip — push, don't pull","Pull it behind you","Kick it to get it rolling","Ask a guest to help"],["Bajarle cosas y dar otra vuelta; empújalo, no lo jales","Jalarlo detrás de ti","Patearlo para que avance","Pedirle ayuda a un huésped"],
 "A reasonable load you push is easier on your body and lets you see where you're going.","Empujar una carga razonable cuida tu cuerpo y te deja ver por dónde vas.",LIFT)
n(RA,"privacy","easy","A room has the Do Not Disturb sign up at checkout time. What do you do?","Un cuarto tiene el letrero de No Molestar a la hora de salida. ¿Qué haces?",
 ["Don't knock or enter; let the front desk or supervisor follow up","Knock loudly until they answer","Enter quietly to check","Skip it and never report it"],["No tocar ni entrar; que la recepción o tu supervisora le den seguimiento","Tocar fuerte hasta que contesten","Entrar despacito a revisar","Saltarlo y no reportarlo"],
 "Respect the sign, but report it so the hotel can do a welfare check per policy.","Respeta el letrero, pero repórtalo para que el hotel haga una revisión de bienestar según la política.",BP)
n(RA,"privacy","med","A guest left their laptop open with banking on the screen. What do you do?","Un huésped dejó su laptop abierta con su banco en la pantalla. ¿Qué haces?",
 ["Don't touch or read it; clean around it","Close it to protect it","Move it to the closet","Take a photo for security"],["No tocarla ni leerla; limpiar alrededor","Cerrarla para protegerla","Guardarla en el clóset","Tomarle foto para seguridad"],
 "Guest belongings and information are private. Clean around personal items without handling them.","Las cosas y la información del huésped son privadas. Limpia alrededor sin tocarlas.",BP)
n(RA,"security","easy","Someone in the hallway says it's their room and asks you to let them in. What do you do?","Alguien en el pasillo dice que es su cuarto y te pide que le abras. ¿Qué haces?",
 ["Politely send them to the front desk for a new key","Open it since they seem nice","Open it if they know the room number","Lend them your master key"],["Mandarlo amablemente a recepción por una llave nueva","Abrirle porque se ve buena gente","Abrirle si sabe el número de cuarto","Prestarle tu llave maestra"],
 "Never open a room for anyone. The desk verifies ID — that protects the real guest.","Nunca le abras un cuarto a nadie. Recepción verifica la identificación, así se protege al huésped real.",BP)
n(RA,"security","med","You lost your master key card during your shift. When do you report it?","Perdiste tu tarjeta llave maestra durante el turno. ¿Cuándo lo reportas?",
 ["Immediately, so it can be deactivated","At the end of the week","Only if you can't find it by tomorrow","No need, it's just a card"],["De inmediato, para que la desactiven","Al final de la semana","Solo si mañana no aparece","No hace falta, es solo una tarjeta"],
 "A lost master opens every room. Fast reporting lets the desk cancel it right away.","Una maestra perdida abre todos los cuartos. Reportarla rápido permite cancelarla de inmediato.",BP)
n(RA,"trafficking","hard","Which pattern could be a sign of human trafficking in a room?","¿Qué situación podría ser señal de trata de personas en un cuarto?",
 ["Many different visitors, DND for days, and a guest who seems controlled or scared","A family with kids' toys","A business traveler with a laptop","Takeout containers in the trash"],["Muchas visitas distintas, No Molestar por días y alguien que parece controlado o con miedo","Una familia con juguetes de niños","Un viajero de negocios con laptop","Envases de comida en la basura"],
 "Don't confront anyone. Note what you saw and tell your manager — they decide whether to call police.","No confrontes a nadie. Anota lo que viste y avísale a tu gerente; ellos deciden si llaman a la policía.",HT)
n(RA,"lostfound","easy","You find a wedding ring by the sink in a checked-out room. What's right?","Encuentras un anillo de boda junto al lavabo en un cuarto ya desocupado. ¿Qué es lo correcto?",
 ["Turn it in to lost and found with the room number, date and time","Keep it if no one calls in a day","Leave it on the counter","Give it to a coworker"],["Entregarlo a objetos perdidos con número de cuarto, fecha y hora","Quedártelo si nadie llama en un día","Dejarlo en el lavabo","Dárselo a un compañero"],
 "Logging lost items with details helps return them and protects you.","Registrar los objetos perdidos con detalles ayuda a devolverlos y te protege a ti.",BP)
n(RA,"cleaning","med","In what order should you clean a bathroom to avoid spreading germs?","¿En qué orden debes limpiar un baño para no regar gérmenes?",
 ["Cleanest to dirtiest — mirror and sink first, toilet last","Toilet first, then sink with the same cloth","Floor first, then counters","Any order is fine"],["De lo más limpio a lo más sucio: espejo y lavabo primero, el inodoro al final","El inodoro primero y luego el lavabo con el mismo trapo","El piso primero y luego las barras","Cualquier orden sirve"],
 "Working clean to dirty, with separate cloths, keeps toilet germs off sinks and glasses.","Trabajar de limpio a sucio, con trapos separados, evita llevar gérmenes del inodoro al lavabo.",BP)
n(RA,"cleaning","med","Why use color-coded cloths, like one color only for toilets?","¿Para qué sirven los trapos de colores, como uno solo para inodoros?",
 ["So toilet cloths never touch sinks, cups or counters","Because they look nicer","To save detergent","So guests know you cleaned"],["Para que los trapos del inodoro nunca toquen lavabos, vasos ni barras","Porque se ven más bonitos","Para ahorrar detergente","Para que el huésped sepa que limpiaste"],
 "Color coding is a simple way to stop cross-contamination.","Usar colores es una forma sencilla de evitar la contaminación cruzada.",BP)
n(RA,"cleaning","med","A disinfectant label says 10-minute contact time. What does that mean?","La etiqueta de un desinfectante dice 10 minutos de contacto. ¿Qué significa?",
 ["The surface must stay wet that long to kill germs before wiping","Wipe it within 10 seconds","It expires in 10 minutes","Rinse after 10 minutes no matter what"],["La superficie debe quedar mojada ese tiempo para matar gérmenes antes de secar","Secarlo en 10 segundos","Caduca en 10 minutos","Enjuagar a los 10 minutos, pase lo que pase"],
 "Wiping too soon means the disinfectant didn't finish working.","Si secas antes, el desinfectante no terminó de hacer su efecto.","https://www.epa.gov/pesticide-registration/selected-eparegistered-disinfectants")
n(RA,"cleaning","easy","Which high-touch item do guests notice most when it's dirty?","¿Qué cosa que se toca mucho notan más los huéspedes cuando está sucia?",
 ["The TV remote — wipe it every room","The ceiling","The back of the closet","The fire sprinkler"],["El control de la tele: límpialo en cada cuarto","El techo","El fondo del clóset","El rociador contra incendios"],
 "Remotes, light switches, handles and phones are high-touch spots to disinfect every time.","Controles, apagadores, manijas y teléfonos se tocan mucho y hay que desinfectarlos siempre.",BP)
n(RA,"maintenance","easy","The bathroom fan is loud and rattling. What do you do?","El extractor del baño hace mucho ruido. ¿Qué haces?",
 ["Report it to maintenance with a work order before the next guest","Ignore it","Try to fix it yourself with a knife","Turn off the breaker"],["Reportarlo a mantenimiento con una orden de trabajo antes del siguiente huésped","Ignorarlo","Intentar arreglarlo con un cuchillo","Bajar el breaker"],
 "You're the eyes of the hotel. Reporting small issues keeps rooms sellable and guests happy.","Tú eres los ojos del hotel. Reportar detalles mantiene los cuartos vendibles y a los huéspedes contentos.",BP)
n(RA,"maintenance","med","There's water on the floor under the sink. What's needed?","Hay agua en el piso debajo del lavabo. ¿Qué se necesita?",
 ["Dry it, put up a wet-floor sign and report a possible leak to maintenance","Just mop it","Put a towel down and leave it","Tell the next guest"],["Secarla, poner letrero de piso mojado y reportar posible fuga a mantenimiento","Solo trapear","Poner una toalla y dejarla","Decirle al siguiente huésped"],
 "Leaks get worse and cause slips. Clean up, warn, and report.","Las fugas empeoran y provocan resbalones. Limpia, avisa y reporta.",SLIP)
n(RA,"guest","easy","A guest asks you for extra towels while you're in the hall. Best response?","Un huésped te pide toallas extra mientras estás en el pasillo. ¿Qué es lo mejor?",
 ["Smile and hand them over from your cart, or bring them quickly","Tell them to call the desk","Say you're busy","Point to the laundry room"],["Sonreír y dárselas de tu carrito o llevárselas rápido","Decirle que llame a recepción","Decirle que estás ocupada","Señalarle la lavandería"],
 "Small, quick yeses make big impressions on guest reviews.","Los pequeños \"sí\" rápidos causan gran impresión en las reseñas.",BP)
n(RA,"cleaning","hard","What do you do with drinking glasses in a stayover room?","¿Qué haces con los vasos en un cuarto ocupado (stayover)?",
 ["Swap them for clean, sealed glasses per standard","Rinse them in the bathroom sink","Leave the used ones","Dry them with the bath towel"],["Cambiarlos por vasos limpios y sellados según el estándar","Enjuagarlos en el lavabo","Dejar los usados","Secarlos con la toalla de baño"],
 "Glasses should never be washed in a guest bathroom — swap them for clean ones.","Los vasos nunca se lavan en el baño del cuarto; se cambian por limpios.",BP)
n(RA,"safety","med","A guest's pet is loose in a room you need to clean. What do you do?","La mascota de un huésped anda suelta en el cuarto que vas a limpiar. ¿Qué haces?",
 ["Don't enter; note it and let the desk contact the guest","Go in and shoo it into the bathroom","Feed it","Take it to the lobby"],["No entrar; anotarlo y que recepción contacte al huésped","Entrar y meterla al baño","Darle de comer","Llevarla al lobby"],
 "For your safety and the pet's, wait until the guest is there or the pet is crated.","Por tu seguridad y la de la mascota, espera a que el huésped esté o que la mascota esté en su jaula.",BP)
n(RA,"winter","easy","It's January and a guest room is freezing with the window cracked open. What do you do?","Es enero y un cuarto está helado con la ventana entreabierta. ¿Qué haces?",
 ["Close the window, set the thermostat to standard and report it if the heat isn't working","Leave it, the guest wanted it","Open it more to air it out","Turn on the oven"],["Cerrar la ventana, poner el termostato en el estándar y reportar si la calefacción no sirve","Dejarla, así la quería el huésped","Abrirla más para ventilar","Prender el horno"],
 "Minnesota cold can freeze pipes near windows. Close it and report heating problems.","El frío de Minnesota puede congelar tuberías cerca de las ventanas. Ciérrala y reporta fallas de calefacción.",COLD,("11-15","03-15"))
n(SUP,"inspection","med","A room fails inspection for hair in the tub. Best approach with the attendant?","Un cuarto no pasa la inspección por pelos en la tina. ¿Cómo lo manejas con la recamarista?",
 ["Show them privately, have it fixed, and coach on the checklist","Call them out in the hallway","Fix it yourself and say nothing","Write them up for the first miss"],["Mostrárselo en privado, que lo corrija y repasar la lista de revisión","Llamarle la atención en el pasillo","Arreglarlo tú y no decir nada","Levantarle un reporte a la primera"],
 "Private, specific coaching fixes the habit without embarrassing anyone.","Corregir en privado y con detalles cambia el hábito sin avergonzar a nadie.",BP)
n(SUP,"inspection","med","Which rooms should be inspected first?","¿Qué cuartos se deben inspeccionar primero?",
 ["Rooms needed for early arrivals or VIPs","The room farthest from the elevator","Whatever is on the top floor","Rooms with DND"],["Los que se necesitan para llegadas tempranas o VIPs","El cuarto más lejos del elevador","Lo que esté en el último piso","Los cuartos con No Molestar"],
 "Prioritize what the front desk needs to sell or assign soon.","Prioriza lo que recepción necesita vender o asignar pronto.",BP)
n(SUP,"staffing","hard","Two attendants called out and checkouts are high. What's the best first move?","Dos recamaristas faltaron y hay muchas salidas. ¿Qué es lo primero que conviene hacer?",
 ["Prioritize arrivals and checkouts, tell the GM and front desk, and split boards fairly","Clean stayovers first","Wait and see","Tell everyone to rush and skip inspections"],["Priorizar llegadas y salidas, avisar al gerente y a recepción, y repartir los cuartos de forma justa","Limpiar primero los stayovers","Esperar a ver qué pasa","Decirle a todos que se apuren y no inspeccionar"],
 "Communicate early and focus on the rooms the hotel needs to sell today.","Comunica temprano y enfócate en los cuartos que el hotel necesita vender hoy.",BP)
n(SUP,"safety","med","An attendant says their back hurts after lifting a mattress. What do you do?","Una recamarista dice que le duele la espalda después de levantar un colchón. ¿Qué haces?",
 ["Have them stop, report the injury to the manager and document it the same day","Tell them to keep going","Give them painkillers","Wait to report until it gets worse"],["Que se detenga, reportar la lesión al gerente y documentarla el mismo día","Decirle que siga","Darle pastillas para el dolor","Esperar a reportarlo hasta que empeore"],
 "Work injuries must be reported promptly so the employee gets proper care.","Las lesiones de trabajo se reportan a tiempo para que la persona reciba atención.","https://www.dli.mn.gov/workers-compensation")
n(SUP,"inventory","med","What do linen par levels tell you?","¿Qué te dicen los niveles par de ropa de cama?",
 ["How many sets you need on hand across rooms, laundry and shelves to run smoothly","The towel color","How many stains are allowed","How many a guest can take home"],["Cuántos juegos se necesitan entre cuartos, lavandería y anaqueles para operar bien","El color de las toallas","Cuántas manchas se permiten","Cuántas puede llevarse un huésped"],
 "Running below par means rooms wait on linen. Track it and order before you're short.","Estar por debajo del par hace que los cuartos esperen ropa. Llévalo controlado y pide antes de que falte.",BP)
